he provider-wide restart protocol is substantially complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart observation, an acknowledged reboot, a different independently corroborated boot identity, and recovered audit service, audit data, saved configuration, and overall system state.","limitations":["Post-reboot `auditctl -s` reported `lost 181`, so recovery evidence is not entirely pristine even though auditing was enabled, auditd was active, the audit log was nonempty, and the system reported `running` (cmd-3b6bf103d71f4be5, cmd-3250c5c2810944c4)."]}
